Observed distinct state defect:
  After successful display cleanup, NativePreparation.cleanup() cleared _display_budget and _display_calibration but left _display_profile. A later fresh diagnostic therefore carried a previous_display with previous_calibration=None. RendererEngine.close_display_calibration() cannot confirm closure for that owner because it requires a previous calibration whenever previous_display is non-None. A failed source cleanup correctly retains all prior fields.
  The separate rig run ended with renderer exit code 0 and no faulthandler error. This cleanup-state defect is not claimed to cause that process exit during OpenDisplayCalibration.

